---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Seishinkai Karate Federation Atsubetsu Branch"
  description="Information about the Seishinkai Atsubetsu Branch in Atsubetsu Ward, Sapporo. View class schedules, venue information, and karate classes for children, families, and adults."
  lang="en"
  path="/en/dojo/atsubetsu/atsubetsu/"
>
  <section class="dojo-list">
    <div class="page-container">
      <div class="section__title-area">
        <span class="section-label">DOJO</span>
        <h1 class="section-title">Seishinkai Karate Federation Atsubetsu Branch</h1>
      </div>

      <h2 class="detail-page__heading">Atsubetsu Karate Classes</h2>

      <div class="detail-page__img-text-pair--reverse">
        <div class="detail-media--med">
          <figure>
            <img
              src="/assets/images/dojo/img_atsubetsu_4.jpg"
              alt="Atsubetsu West Community Centre"
              width="234"
              height="144"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </div>

        <p>
          The Atsubetsu Karate Class began training at the Atsubetsu West
          Community Centre in April 1993.<br />
          Since its establishment, the dojo has welcomed everyone from young
          children to adults, offering karate classes for children, juniors, and
          families.<br />
          Families are especially encouraged to train together.<br />
          Branch Chief Wakabayashi and his son also joined Seishinkai as a
          parent-and-child team and now lead the branch together.<br />
          While many dojos focus on a highly competitive sports-club atmosphere,
          our goal is to provide enjoyable karate training that promotes health,
          fitness, and lifelong learning in a friendly club environment.<br />
          <strong>Class ① is intended for beginners.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="detail-page__heading">Friday Classes</h2>

      <div class="detail-page__img-text-pair--reverse">
        <div class="detail-media--big">
          <figure>
            <img
              src="/assets/images/dojo/img_atsubetsu_1.jpg"
              alt="Friday karate class"
              width="234"
              height="144"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="detail-media">
            <figure>
              <img
                src="/assets/images/instructors/tsubasa.jpg"
                alt="Instructor Tsubasa Okubo"
                width="234"
                height="144"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </figure>
            <figcaption>Directly Operated by Headquarters</figcaption>
          </div>

          <p>
            ① 6:00 pm – 7:00 pm<br />
            ② 7:10 pm – 8:10 pm<br />
            (Hall available until 8:30 pm)
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="detail-page__heading">Sunday Classes</h2>

      <div class="detail-page__img-text-pair--reverse">
        <div class="detail-media--big">
          <figure>
            <img
              src="/assets/images/dojo/img_atsubetsu_2.jpg"
              alt="Sunday karate class"
              width="234"
              height="144"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="detail-media">
            <figure>
              <img
                src="/assets/images/instructors/wakabayashi.jpg"
                alt="Branch Chief Wakabayashi"
                width="234"
                height="144"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </figure>
          </div>

          <p>
            ① 9:30 am – 10:30 am<br />
            ② 10:40 am – 11:50 am<br />
            <br />
            <strong>Winter Schedule (December–March)</strong><br />
            ① 10:00 am – 10:50 am<br />
            ② 11:00 am – 11:55 am
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="detail-page__heading">Atsubetsu Branch Information</h2>

      <p class="detail-page__note">
        <strong>Established:</strong> April 1993<br />
        <strong>Founder:</strong> Katsumi Okubo<br />
        <strong>Instructors:</strong> Keiji Wakabayashi, Shirakawa,<br />
        Tsubasa Okubo, Masuda, and Saito
      </p>

      <h2 class="detail-page__heading">Training Venue</h2>

      <p>
        Atsubetsu West Community Centre<br />
        2F Meeting Room<br />
        10-1 Atsubetsu Nishi 4-jo 4-chome, Atsubetsu-ku, Sapporo
      </p>

      <div class="dojo-list__map-embed">
        <iframe
          src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d2915.450311471158!2d141.46572229999998!3d43.05299579999999!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x5f0b2c7d48b71893%3A0x7e0fefb1cdf04351!2z44CSMDA0LTAwNjQgSG9ra2FpZG8sIFNhcHBvcm8sIEF0c3ViZXRzdSBXYXJkLCBBdHN1YmV0c3UgTmlzaGkgNCBKxY0sIDQtY2jFjW1l4oiSMTDiiJIxIOacreW5jOW4guWOmuWIpeilv-WcsOWMuuOCu-ODs-OCv-ODvA!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjp!4v1785048971458!5m2!1sen!2sjp"
          width="600"
          height="450"
          style="border:0;"
          allowfullscreen=""
          loading="lazy"
          referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
        ></iframe>
      </div>

      <p class="detail-page__note">
        As this is a public facility, please contact the Seishinkai office
        rather than the venue for enquiries.
      </p>

      <p class="detail-page__note">
        If the Atsubetsu West Community Centre is unavailable, training may be
        held at Oasa Seishinkan or the Kawashimo Co-op 2F Circle Room.
      </p>

      <p class="detail-page__note">
        <a href="mailto:karate@seishinkan.ne.jp?subject=Atsubetsu%20Trial%20Lesson%20Enquiry">
          <img
            src="/assets/images/dojo/img_atsubetsu_3.jpg"
            alt="Apply for a Trial Class"
            width="645"
            height="293"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
      </p>

      <p class="detail-page__back">
        <a href="/en/dojo/atsubetsu/">
          ← Back to Atsubetsu Ward Dojos
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>